#!/usr/bin/env bash
# SUPERSEDED. Use the copy inside the environment you mean to publish:
#
#     <repo>/bin/refresh-homers-lotr-wiki [--publish]
#
# This file used to be a full wiki-build runner with the season-1 values baked
# in: --base-url https://homerslotr.com/, season 1's run dir as --log-dir,
# --max-character-level 40, and no roadmap or --publish steps at all. It was
# already stale when there were two environments. There are now three - a
# permanent dev realm, the live season and an archived season - and a
# season-blind wiki build is not merely out of date, it is a live hazard:
#
#   * --base-url decides the absolute URLs written into every generated page,
#     so building the wrong one silently produces a site that links to another
#     realm's wiki throughout;
#   * --log-dir and --db-dir decide WHOSE kill counts, server-firsts and
#     activity charts the pages report, so a mis-scoped build publishes one
#     season's player statistics under another season's name;
#   * --max-character-level 40 is simply wrong everywhere now (the cap is 60).
#
# There is no correct default to fall back to, which is exactly why this
# refuses instead of guessing. Each repo's own copy derives all of it from that
# repo's server.env and is relocatable (PROJECT comes from BASH_SOURCE), so the
# environment is implied by the path you invoke.
#
# See season-cutover-guide.md, and season-cutover-prereqs.md item 4.
set -euo pipefail

cat >&2 <<'EOF'
refresh-homers-lotr-wiki: this shared copy is superseded and does nothing.

Run the wiki build from the environment you actually mean, e.g.

    ~/GIT/nwn_homers_lotr/bin/refresh-homers-lotr-wiki              # dev realm
    ~/GIT/nwn_homers_lotr_s2/bin/refresh-homers-lotr-wiki --publish # live season
    ~/GIT/nwn_homers_lotr_s1/bin/refresh-homers-lotr-wiki --publish # archived

Each derives its base URL, log dir, database dir and level cap from that
repo's own server.env. This copy had season 1's values hardcoded and would
publish one realm's statistics under another realm's URLs.
EOF
exit 2
